course: dictionary
lesson: 5519
title: Leap into meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Leap has more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one is meant. «Springboks leap high with stiff legs» means they jump. «Leap at the chance» is a phrase meaning to accept something eagerly.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. «February has 28 days, or 29 in a leap year.» The word year tells you a leap year is a special kind of year, not a jump. Ask yourself: does the jump idea fit here? If not, look for other clues.
explain: Try swapping in your meaning. In «Sifakas are lemurs built for leaping between trees», jump fits well, so leaping means jumping from tree to tree. Use this swap check for every new word you meet.
fact: To leap means to jump high or far, or to move or act suddenly.
fact: A leap is a big jump, or a big sudden change.
fact: A leap year has 366 days, with an extra day at the end of February.
fact: «Sifakas» are lemurs that leap between trees, and they bounce sideways on the ground.
fact: «Leap at the chance» means to accept it eagerly.
exercise: «Manta rays sometimes leap right out of the sea.» What does leap mean here? | To sleep in the sea | To swim very slowly | *To jump high or far | To wash clean
exercise: «February has 28 days, or 29 in a leap year.» How many days does a leap year have? | 29 | 300 | *366 | 365
exercise: Nadia says, «She will leap at the chance to join the team.» What does leap at the chance mean? | *Accept it eagerly | Jump over a fence to get there | Run away from the chance | Forget it quickly
test: «Prices took a leap forward this year.» What does leap mean in this sentence? | Jump over a wall | *A big sudden change | Sleep deeply | Sing softly
test: Which word means the same as jump in «Springboks leap high with stiff legs»? | *Spring | Crawl | Hide | Sit
exam: Which statement about a leap year is true? | It has 365 days | It has 29 days in total | It has no February | *It has 366 days, with an extra day at the end of February
